From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mjackson <mjackson@microsoft.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:11:34 -0700
Subject: Prevent tainted canvas image exports through the clipboard

Require an origin-clean canvas before exporting a clipboard snapshot or
image data URL. ImageFromNode() returns null for a non-OriginClean()
canvas (no bitmap snapshot) and HTMLCanvasElement::ImageSourceURL()
returns empty for a tainted canvas (blocks the data-URL markup and
Save-image). ContextMenuController sets has_image_contents from
OriginClean() so "Copy image / Save image to" are greyed out.

Adds tests to assert a cross-origin-tainted canvas writes nothing, and
preserves existing clipboard contents while a clean canvas still writes
its full snapshot.

Also completed manual testing of changes.

Bug: 574640036
Change-Id: I56e33048f20ec5d4d2fe2fb302f1d7b6d6e365e7
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8614470
Commit-Queue: Mike Jackson <mjackson@microsoft.com>
Reviewed-by: Dan Clark <daniec@microsoft.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1725289}

